        "id": "p75-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Explain why it is impossible for the perimeter to be 17.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{1}{3}$ would make a side length negative.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x+18&=17\\\\3x&=-1\\\\x&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThis would make the side lengths $x$ and $2x$ negative, which is impossible.",
